    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The nurse sets up the following equation: <span data-math=\"D\\;÷\\;H\\; \\times \\;Q\\; = \\;A\"></span>. <span data-math=\"D\"></span> represents the desired dose (the dose ordered), <span data-math=\"H\"></span> the amount on hand or available, \n<span data-math=\"Q\"></span> the quantity or volume of the drug form (tablet, capsule, liquid), and <span data-math=\"A\"></span> the amount calculated to be administered to the client. Therefore, <span data-math=\"1250\\;\\text{units/hour}\\;÷\\;25{,}000\\;\\text{units}\\times500\\;\\text{mL}\\; = \\;25\\;\\text{mL/hour}\"></span>."
    }
   ],
